{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/cases/peka-as-personal-representative-of-the-estate-of-ida-hawkins-v-te-hei", "captured_at": "2026-06-12T06:23:57.656507+00:00", "content": "Peka as personal representative of the estate of Ida Hawkins v Te Hei", "content_hash": "4ea8c00126466f19724b68e9412641e881ff1609623a76dbed57b4421d850495", "cross_source_ids": {"feed_entry_id": "94a2644252b177cd5bcf0733", "feed_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/the-courts/supreme-court/judgments-supreme/RSS"}, "extraction_method": "feedparser", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2025-08-24T12:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/rss/2025-08/61573464eef453f7d631fa0c.json", "record_id": "rss:61573464eef453f7d631fa0c", "source_account": "courtsofnz.govt.nz", "source_kind": "rss_entry", "source_platform": "rss", "source_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/the-courts/supreme-court/judgments-supreme/RSS"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/cases/r-v-tupou", "captured_at": "2026-06-12T06:23:53.256577+00:00", "content": "R v Tupou\n\n<p>Sentencing - the offender had pleaded guilty to charges of murder and being in unlawful possession of a firearm - the offender and the victim came from families who had been engaged in a long-running feud with each other - this had resulted in numerous outbreaks of violence involving the use of firearms - the offender encountered the victim by chance when he arrived at a liquor store - he went to the victim's vehicle and shot him on two occasions whilst he was sitting in the driver's seat of the vehicle - there was no dispute that a sentence of life imprisonment was appropriate - starting point for minimum term of imprisonment of 12 and a half years to reflect the aggravating features of the offending - discount of one year to reflect guilty pleas and six months to reflect relative youth (23 years) and expressions of remorse - end sentence life imprisonment with a minimum term of 11 years.</p>", "content_hash": "d7a3d696d1bfd21cb8591922560b94e843c80b452631cbcd012af2d043e94d4c", "cross_source_ids": {"feed_entry_id": "7889ab51787be00a09c82779", "feed_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/judgments/high-court/RSS"}, "extraction_method": "feedparser", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2025-08-12T12:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/rss/2025-08/63cea781169d719881c86a86.json", "record_id": "rss:63cea781169d719881c86a86", "source_account": "courtsofnz.govt.nz", "source_kind": "rss_entry", "source_platform": "rss", "source_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/judgments/high-court/RSS"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/cases/huljich-v-r-1", "captured_at": "2026-06-12T06:23:57.670256+00:00", "content": "Huljich v R", "content_hash": "3f2a4189409752c26f7bf28cacaffd62e6f5783963196f25a377d11474d1f6ed", "cross_source_ids": {"feed_entry_id": "7a6e8ba461ed5a19a591bd07", "feed_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/the-courts/supreme-court/judgments-supreme/RSS"}, "extraction_method": "feedparser", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2025-08-05T12:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/rss/2025-08/6b1c3fc4377ff2a9c912cc84.json", "record_id": "rss:6b1c3fc4377ff2a9c912cc84", "source_account": "courtsofnz.govt.nz", "source_kind": "rss_entry", "source_platform": "rss", "source_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/the-courts/supreme-court/judgments-supreme/RSS"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/cases/r-v-mcleod", "captured_at": "2026-06-12T06:23:53.254329+00:00", "content": "R v McLeod\n\n<p>Sentencing for murder under ss 167 and 172 of the Crimes Act 1961. Defendant had entered a property at night and stabbed the victim with a knife while he was sleeping, with an apparent motive of jealousy. <br /><br />Defendant sentenced to life imprisonment with a minimum period of imprisonment of 17 years due to the operation of s 104 of the Sentencing Act 2002. Two aggravating factors under s 104(1A) were engaged: unlawful entry into a dwelling place and the victim's unconscious state making him \"particularly vulnerable\". There was no manifest injustice in a minimum period of imprisonment of 17 years. </p>", "content_hash": "54762eada7b332b5ff83da8cba9be805be33a4571ad1d468b73f406ac16e4d5f", "cross_source_ids": {"feed_entry_id": "1eb1f94d330df38873150fff", "feed_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/judgments/high-court/RSS"}, "extraction_method": "feedparser", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2025-08-12T12:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/rss/2025-08/99b11eb8918cae00ac950e12.json", "record_id": "rss:99b11eb8918cae00ac950e12", "source_account": "courtsofnz.govt.nz", "source_kind": "rss_entry", "source_platform": "rss", "source_url": "https://www.courtsofnz.govt.nz/judgments/high-court/RSS"}
